WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.800
You never know what will
happen to a story like this.

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:04.680
You never know
how it will resonate.

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:06.000
You just pray.

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:07.560
To the Nordic gods,
of course.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.760
If we wanted to describe...

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:19.880
basically you could say
the problems

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:22.840
that every young person

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:26.720
could actually
be facing in real life.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:27.880
But, of course,

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:31.440
adding this supernatural
element to the story

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.400
that this young kid

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:36.880
actually has the makings
of a god inside him.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:41.080
We have been looking at
the whole season.

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:45.000
That is basically the first
structure we're working on.

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:47.880
Where is Magne at the
beginning of the season,

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:49.600
where does he end?

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:53.560
And how do we split
this huge development

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:57.440
over a six
natural part structure.

00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:59.600
That is the first structure
we're looking at.

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:02.200
Then we're delving into
every single episode.

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:03.880
And, of course,
in every single episode,

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:05.520
every single scene

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:09.720
and find our way the natural
structure for the episode.

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:12.200
Being a writer,
that very much likes this

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:15.320
gritty-realism
that is very significant

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.880
for much story telling
in the Nordic countries.

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:19.680
It was a joy for me
actually,

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:22.600
to go into
the supernatural genre

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:25.000
and all of the sudden,
you know, discussing

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:26.760
"Can this character fly?"

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:29.080
It was amazing,

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:34.080
to have all these
possibilities on your table.

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:40.680
At all times
you have to be focused

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:43.200
on the forces of antagonism.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:48.040
That your main character
has enough against him.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:51.320
One of the most
difficult things

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:53.160
to write about the show
was probably

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:57.960
the moment you begin to
put in supernatural elements

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:00.200
in a realistic world.

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:03.880
You really need to set up
all the rules about this.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:07.680
Because how much
a god is he?

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:12.480
How far can his abilities,

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.640
where they are now,
actually take him?

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:20.920
There's a very important
theme in Ragnarok,

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.080
which is the environmental
theme.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.800
We thought that was very
interesting to throw in.

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:26.680
Not only because

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:30.200
it is a very modern
element in all our lives,

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:31.880
so all these discussions

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:34.880
that they are actually
having in Ragnarok,

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:37.760
are very much discussions

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:40.160
that I'm having myself
on the private scene.

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:42.520
I think, as a writer,
it's extremely important

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:44.960
to remind yourself
at all times

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:48.120
that you cannot write
for everyone.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:51.440
You cannot write a story
for 190 countries.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:55.240
Because I think if you try
to write for everyone,

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:57.520
you will end up
writing for no one.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:02.240
See you. Bye bye.

